// ============================================================================
// VaultLaunch — XelisVault Protocol
// ============================================================================
// A serious, self-contained launchpad for XEL. Real projects only: every
// launch is filtered by a community validation vote, priced by a
// constant-product bonding curve, and held to a long-term community trust
// standard (Trusted / Untrusted). NOT a memecoin casino — the vote window is
// the quality filter, and the trust system keeps founders accountable long
// after graduation.
//
// v2.0 — TWO-PATH GRADUATION (D7): a founder who locks serious liquidity
// from day one (>= direct_listing_threshold) graduates DIRECTLY; smaller
// floats discover price on the bonding curve first. Graduation is worth
// reaching: graduated projects trade at a LOWER fee (D8) and the team
// allocation unlocks (D3). A small migration fee is taken from the curve
// once, at graduation (D9).
//
// v3.0 — FULL PROPOSAL DATA (D10): the vote happens with EVERYTHING on the
// table — the creator declares a vesting plan AT PROPOSITION TIME and the
// contract enforces it at graduation. Projects carry SOCIAL LINKS
// (Twitter / Telegram / Discord, D11) the team can update at any time. And
// the contract keeps the market's scoreboard (D12): per-project buy/sell
// volume, trade count, spot market cap, ATH and the graduation snapshot
// are all calculated and STORED on-chain.
//
// v4.0 — REAL ASSETS, REAL MIGRATION. Every launched token is now a TRUE
// XELIS confidential asset (D13): created by the contract at validation
// success via Asset::create with MaxSupplyMode::Fixed — the ENTIRE supply
// exists from birth, is held by the contract, and can NEVER be minted past
// its cap (the cap is enforced by the XELIS protocol itself, not by our
// code). The bonding curve trades REAL tokens (D14): buys transfer actual
// assets to the buyer's wallet, sells consume the buyer's attached token
// deposit — no internal ledger anywhere. And graduation now really means
// migration (D15): the curve's XEL reserves and its remaining token
// inventory move ATOMICALLY into a permanent LaunchDEX pool via one
// cross-contract call with attached deposits. Buyers hold their tokens in
// their own wallets from the first second, can transfer them freely
// anywhere on XELIS, and keep trading them on the DEX long after the
// launchpad's job is done.
//
// ONE launchpad contract + ONE pinned DEX contract. No other dependencies.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// DESIGN DECISIONS (and why — read before changing anything)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// D1. (v4, supersedes v1's internal ledger) REAL CONFIDENTIAL ASSETS. The
//     token of every validated project is a native XELIS asset created by
//     this contract at finalize_validation (D13) — buyers' balances live in
//     their own wallets, are fully confidential at the base layer, and are
//     usable by every wallet/exchange/service on XELIS. Nothing is owed to
//     the launchpad: what you bought is yours, transferable from the first
//     block.
//
// D2. (v4, supersedes v2's "the contract IS the venue") GRADUATION IS A
//     REAL MIGRATION. When a project graduates, its XEL reserves and token
//     inventory move to a permanent LaunchDEX pool (D15/D16). Between
//     graduation and migration the curve keeps serving trades at the
//     reduced graduated fee (D8) — a slow admin never strands a hot
//     project — and migrate() (permissionless, anyone) executes the move
//     atomically. After migration the curve is closed; all trading happens
//     on the DEX at the DEX fee.
//
// D3. Team tokens are RESERVED from day one and CLAIMED after graduation.
//     The curve's sellable supply excludes the team allocation from day
//     one, so the allocation can never be over-sold. Once the project
//     graduates, the creator chooses: claim the full allocation immediately
//     (the migration reward) OR lock it into a linear vesting (a public
//     commitment signal — visible to every buyer via get_team_allocation).
//     A project that never graduates does not hold the team hostage: after
//     team_unlock_delay (~6 months) of bonding, the creator may claim the
//     allocation late. Claims are debited against a running team_paid
//     counter — the allocation is paid EXACTLY once across all paths (I4).
//     v4: claims pay REAL tokens from the contract's escrow (the launchpad
//     retains exactly team_remaining after migration — I10), and the claim
//     event carries NO amount (the payout is a native confidential
//     transfer; only the creator sees it — D18).
//
// D4. Losing trust blocks BUYS, never SELLs. When a project is Untrusted,
//     new buys are refused (protecting new entrants) but holders can
//     always exit. v4 extends this across the migration: the DEX pool's
//     BUYS can be paused (sync_trust_to_dex) while its sells stay open
//     forever — a trust flip can never trap funds, on either venue.
//
// D5. Fees ACCRUE and are pulled by withdraw_fees(). Submission, trading,
//     migration and recovery fees accumulate in `pending_fees`; the admin
//     withdraws them capped at what the contract can spare after covering
//     every curve's reserves, every refundable rejection and every
//     earmarked asset budget. 100% of revenue goes to the admin — nothing
//     is burned.
//
// D6. Voting is 1 address = 1 vote, per voting round. Every vote costs a
//     network fee — and, when the admin raises the D21 dial, a REFUNDABLE
//     XEL deposit. Votes reset when a new validation round opens; trust
//     tallies otherwise accumulate for the whole life of the project.
//
// D7. TWO-PATH GRADUATION (the liquidity cap). A founder may lock ANY
//     liquidity >= min_liquidity; whether the project skips the bonding
//     phase is decided by the DIRECT LISTING THRESHOLD, an admin-tunable
//     cap (default 2000 XEL). Liquidity >= threshold at propose time means
//     the project graduates the moment validation passes: asset creation,
//     migration fee and a same-block pool seeding (deep reserves,
//     graduated fee, Trusted badge, team unlock — the full set of
//     graduation advantages, immediately). Below the threshold: the
//     classic bonding curve and its price discovery. The threshold is
//     snapshotted per project at propose time (founders get the rules
//     they signed up for), and it can never undercut min_liquidity
//     (cross-checked setters).
//
// D8. GRADUATION PAYS. Between graduation and migration the curve trades
//     at graduated_fee_bps (default 0.25%) instead of trading_fee_bps
//     (default 0.50% while bonding); after migration the DEX's own fee
//     (default 0.30%) applies. The setters cross-check graduated_fee_bps
//     <= trading_fee_bps and the fee helper re-clamps at read time, so
//     the graduation discount can never be inverted by any parameter
//     combination. The discount is acquired at graduation and survives a
//     later trust loss (holders exit cheap; the milestone is what is
//     rewarded, not ongoing behaviour).
//
// D9. MIGRATION FEE — protocol revenue at migration, pump.fun-style but
//     small: when a project graduates — by curve growth OR by direct
//     listing — migration_fee_bps (default 0.5%) is taken ONCE from the
//     project's curve reserves and accrues to pending_fees (admin
//     revenue, D5). Charged on the reserves AT the graduation moment, so
//     a direct listing pays it on its seed liquidity and a curve graduate
//     on its (>= 4x larger) grown reserves. What is left is exactly what
//     migrate() will seed the pool with.
//
// D10. VESTING PLAN AT PROPOSITION — the votable commitment. propose()
//     takes a vesting_duration: 0 means "team claims at graduation", any
//     value inside the admin-bounded window [vesting_min, vesting_max] is
//     a DECLARED PLAN that the contract BINDS at graduation: graduate()
//     starts the linear vesting automatically with exactly that duration.
//     The community votes with the unlock schedule on the table
//     (get_proposal_data exposes it before a single vote is cast); a
//     creator cannot water the commitment down afterwards. The plan is
//     validated against the bounds snapshotted at propose time and only
//     binds at graduation: a project that never graduates falls back to
//     the late-claim path (D3).
//
// D11. SOCIAL LINKS — mutable project metadata. Twitter, Telegram and
//     Discord links are part of the proposal (empty = "no link") and can
//     be updated by the creator AT ANY TIME via update_project_info,
//     exactly like description/website/logo. Name/symbol/supply/team stay
//     immutable (structural) — the symbol is moreover RESERVED in the
//     launchpad's ticker registry at propose time (first project wins it;
//     chain-wide, XELIS asset tickers are self-declared, so this registry
//     is what keeps launchpad listings unambiguous).
//
// D12. ON-CHAIN TRADING DATA — the contract keeps the scoreboard itself.
//     Every curve buy/sell records: directional volumes, the running
//     total, the trade count, the last trade topoheight — per project AND
//     protocol-wide — plus the spot market cap recomputed and STORED
//     after every trade, its all-time high, and the market cap snapshotted
//     at graduation. v4 scopes this to the CURVE ERA: after migration the
//     curve is closed (its scoreboard freezes) and LaunchDEX keeps the
//     pool-era scoreboard (per-pool volumes, reserves, spot price) — the
//     SDK aggregates both eras for the frontend.
//
// D13. ASSET CREATION AT VALIDATION SUCCESS (not before). The real asset
//     is born the moment the community says yes: failed proposals never
//     pollute the chain with dead assets and never pay the protocol's
//     asset-creation cost. Asset::create is called with the project id as
//     the asset's local id, the proposed name/symbol, 8 decimals (XEL
//     parity, so curve math is unit-honest) and
//     MaxSupplyMode::Fixed { max_supply: total_supply }: the WHOLE supply
//     is minted to this contract at creation and NOBODY — not the admin,
//     not the founder, not this contract — can ever mint one more unit.
//     The chain fee for creating an asset is paid from an EARMARKED
//     BUDGET collected at propose time (asset_budget, admin-tunable):
//     create_project_asset measures the ACTUAL fee by balance-delta
//     (robust to any future fee change), accepts a top-up deposit on the
//     finalize transaction if the chain got more expensive, refunds the
//     unused part to the creator, and verifies on the spot that the full
//     supply actually landed in the contract's balance ("assetbal") —
//     a failed or partial creation reverts the whole finalize.
//
// D14. THE CURVE TRADES REAL TOKENS. buy(pid): attach XEL, receive real
//     tokens in your wallet (a native confidential transfer from the
//     contract's inventory). sell(pid): attach tokens (the WHOLE deposit
//     is sold — symmetric with buy, nothing can be stranded), receive
//     XEL. The curve's state is pure bookkeeping over the contract's real
//     balances, and the identity balance == curve_supply + team_remaining
//     holds at every block (I10) — auditable by anyone, any time.
//
// D15. ATOMIC TWO-STEP MIGRATION. Crossing the graduation threshold (or
//     passing validation as a direct listing) flips the project Graduated
//     — the milestone, the fee discount, the team unlock, the vesting
//     bind — but does NOT touch any funds: the curve keeps trading at the
//     graduated fee until the pool exists (admin-lag tolerant). Then
//     migrate(pid), callable by ANYONE: one transaction that takes the
//     curve's whole XEL reserves and its whole token inventory (team
//     escrow excepted) and seeds a permanent LaunchDEX pool with them, by
//     cross-contract call with attached deposits (Contract::call with a
//     deposits map — the funds and the pool creation are one atomic
//     operation; a failure anywhere reverts everything). The DEX address
//     is admin-pinned and FREEZES at the first migration (a repinned DEX
//     could orphan live pools). After migration the curve is closed
//     forever ("migrated") and the launchpad remains the project's home
//     for votes, socials, trust and team claims.
//
// D16. THE POOL IS PERMANENT (see LaunchDEX X2). Liquidity that migrates
//     can never be withdrawn by anyone — not the admin, not the founder,
//     not the launchpad. This is the anti-rug guarantee: the deeper the
//     pool, the safer the market. Anyone (project, community, protocol)
//     may deepen it further via LaunchDEX add_liquidity — also permanent.
//
// D17. TRUST ACROSS VENUES, WITHOUT PERMISSION TRAPS. Cross-contract
//     calls consume the CALLING transaction's contract-call permission —
//     embedding one inside report/support would force every voter's
//     wallet to grant it. So the trust flip stays a pure launchpad state
//     change, and a separate permissionless entry, sync_trust_to_dex,
//     mirrors it to the pool's buys-pause (keeper bots, a frontend
//     button, or anyone). If the project is Untrusted AT migration time,
//     migrate() pauses the pool's buys in the SAME transaction — no gap.
//     Sells on the pool are never pausable (D4).
//
// D18. PRIVACY, MAXIMALLY. (1) Every launched token is a native XELIS
//     confidential asset: balances and transfer amounts are encrypted at
//     the base layer — invisible to third parties, visible in every
//     wallet, usable everywhere. (2) Team claims pay from escrow via a
//     native confidential transfer and the TeamClaimed event carries NO
//     amount — the payout is the creator's private business. (3) Wallet
//     to wallet trades of launched tokens (outside the launchpad/DEX)
//     inherit XELIS privacy automatically. Honest limitation, by chain
//     design: deposits ATTACHED to contract invocations are public (the
//     contract must read the amount) — curve buys' XEL in, sells' tokens
//     in, and DEX swaps' inputs are therefore public; everything else
//     (wallet balances, transfers, payouts out of contracts) is
//     confidential.
//
// D19. DEX PINNING. set_dex_address (admin) is possible only while NO
//     project has ever migrated; after the first migration the pin is
//     frozen forever (the pools live inside that contract — repointing
//     would orphan them). LaunchDEX mirrors this: its launchpad pin
//     freezes at its first pool. The two cross-called chunk ids
//     (create_pool, set_pool_buys_paused) are PINNED CONSTANTS here and
//     asserted against LaunchDEX's real chunk numbering by CI — renumbering
//     either contract without the other fails the build.
//
// D20. SOUND XEL ACCOUNTING (I2, tightened from v2). total_curve_xel is
//     the exact sum of every live curve's reserves (seeds included — v2
//     left them as slack; migration needs exactness), and
//     locked_refunds + pending_fees + earmarked budgets + locked vote pots
//     complete the committed side. balance >= committed at every block;
//     every path that moves XEL (buy, sell, fee, refund, asset creation,
//     migration, vote deposit/claim) updates both sides in the same
//     transaction.
//
// D21. SYBIL DIAL — REFUNDABLE VOTE DEPOSITS (founder risk review, point
//     5). 1-address-1-vote is free to farm while the community is small
//     (20 wallets decide a validation). XELIS confidentiality rules out
//     balance- or age-weighted voting (nobody can read anyone's balance),
//     so the honest lever is CAPITAL: set_vote_deposit (admin, capped at
//     10 XEL, DEFAULT 0.5 XEL since v4.2 — a refundable participation
//     cost from day one, founder risk review point 2) makes every
//     support()/report() attach that amount; it is LOCKED for the round's
//     duration and fully REFUNDED by claim_vote_deposit(pid, round) once
//     the round has closed
//     (per-voter pull — no unbounded loops; the vote slot itself records
//     the locked amount). An honest voter only ever lends gas-locked
//     capital; a sybil farmer must lock 20x the deposit across wallets and
//     rounds. The dial is a circuit-breaker to raise under attack — and it
//     is documented as a mitigation, not a cure
//     (small communities stay the weak link; min_participants remains the
//     product-side defense).
//
// D22. FRONTEND COMPLETENESS — EVERYTHING THE SITE NEEDS IS ON-CHAIN. The
//     site is static-hosted (Vercel): it stores NOTHING, so the contracts
//     must serve every listing, every stat and every link through views.
//     v4.1 adds the two missing bridges: a REVERSE INDEX asset hash ->
//     project id (get_project_by_asset — the DEX enumerates pools by asset,
//     this maps them back to the launchpad's project pages) and a MIGRATED
//     INDEX (get_migrated_count / get_migrated_by_rank — every project that
//     ever moved to a DEX pool, across DEX generations). Combined with the
//     per-status rankings (get_projects_by_status / get_project_by_rank),
//     the full launchpad surface — validating, bonding, graduated,
//     migrated, trusted, untrusted, rejected — is enumerable in O(list)
//     views, no indexer, no database, no server state.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// LIFECYCLE (status codes)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   0 Validation  project submitted; support/report window is open
//                 (ends at validation_end topoheight; outcome applied by
//                  finalize_validation, callable by ANYONE after the window)
//       ├── pass (>= min_participants voters AND >= 80% support)
//       │     ├── [D13] Asset::create — the REAL token is born (Fixed
//       │     │        supply, whole balance held by this contract)
//       │     ├── liquidity >= direct_listing_threshold ──> 3 Graduated
//       │     │     (direct listing: migration fee taken; the pool can be
//       │     │      seeded the same block via migrate; graduated fee;
//       │     │      Trusted badge; team unlock — D7/D8/D9/D15)
//       │     └── else ──> 2 Bonding (curve is live, real tokens out/in)
//       └── fail ──> 1 Rejected ──> claim_refund() returns 100% of the
//                                    founder's liquidity + asset budget
//   2 Bonding     curve is live: buy() / sell() on REAL assets; votes
//                 continue and can flip the project Untrusted (see D4)
//                 graduation when reserves >= liquidity * multiplier
//                 ──> 3 Graduated (+ Trusted): migration fee taken (D9),
//                     team allocation claimable (D3), curve keeps trading
//                     at the graduated fee until migration (D15)
//   3 Graduated   awaiting migrate() — permissionless, atomic (D15):
//                 curve reserves + token inventory -> permanent LaunchDEX
//                 pool; curve closes ("migrated"); votes, socials, trust
//                 and team claims continue on the launchpad (D3/D11/D17)
//   5 Untrusted   reports reached the loss threshold while Bonding/
//                 Graduated/Trusted: buys blocked (curve AND, once
//                 synced/migrated, pool), sells open everywhere (D4/D17)
//                 recovery: request_revalidation() by the creator —
//                   * not graduated: free, normal thresholds
//                   * graduated: pays recovery_fee (default 250 XEL to
//                     the admin) and must pass STRICTER thresholds
//                   ──> 6 Recovery window ──> pass: 2 (Bonding) or 4 (Trusted)
//                                             fail: back to 5 (retryable)
//   4 Trusted     recovered status for graduated projects (same trading
//                 rules as Graduated)
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// BONDING-CURVE MATH (constant product, integer, contract-favouring floors)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// State per project: R = real XEL reserves, C = curve token supply
// (sellable inventory held by the contract, team allocation excluded).
// Price = R / C.
//
//   buy  with X XEL attached:      fee = X * fee_bps / 10000
//                                  net = X - fee                  (joins R)
//                                  tokens_out = C * net / (R + net)
//   sell of T tokens (attached):   gross = R * T / (C + T)         (leaves R)
//                                  fee  = gross * fee_bps / 10000
//                                  out  = gross - fee              (to caller)
//
//   fee_bps = current_fee_bps(graduated): graduated_fee_bps once the
//   project has graduated (D8, clamped <= trading_fee_bps), else
//   trading_fee_bps. Buy, sell AND both quotes use the same helper, so a
//   quote can never disagree with the trade it previews.
//
// Both directions floor (integer division) in favour of the contract, so the
// curve can never go insolvent from rounding. All intermediates are computed
// in u128 (products are up to 1e31; u64 would overflow).
//
// Graduation (curve path): R >= liquidity_deposited * graduation_multiplier
// (u128 compare), checked after every buy while Bonding. At that moment
// take_migration_fee() applies: fee = fee_take(R, migration_fee_bps);
// R -= fee; pending_fees += fee (D9).
//
// Migration (D15): pool_xel = R (post-fee, net of any pending-window
// sells), pool_tokens = C. Both are attached to the LaunchDEX create_pool
// cross-call; the launchpad keeps ONLY the team escrow (team_remaining).
//
// Team unlock (D3): unlocked =
//   vesting active (vs > 0) : team * (topo - vs) / vd   (linear, floored)
//   graduated, no vesting   : team                      (immediate full)
//   bonding >= team_delay   : team                      (late full claim)
//   otherwise               : 0
// claimable = unlocked - team_paid (paid EXACTLY once across paths — I4).
//
// Market cap = R * (total_supply - C - team_remaining) / C (u128, saturating)
// — the CURVE-ERA cap (D12): after migration the launchpad's stored cap
// freezes at 0 (curve closed, C = 0) and the live cap is the DEX pool's
// price * circulating supply (SDK-composed).
//
// Volume (D12): buy_volume sums the ATTACHED XEL of every buy (fee
// included, like an exchange's quote-side volume), sell_volume sums the
// PRE-FEE gross XEL out of every sell, total volume = buy + sell. Kept per
// project (bv/sv/vo) and protocol-wide (tbv/tsv/tvl), with trade counts
// (tc/ttc) and the last trade topoheight (lt). I9 keeps the identity
// vo == bv + sv exact at all times.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// FEES (defaults — ALL admin-configurable, ALL revenue to the admin)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   submission_fee             10 XEL     paid once per proposal (non-refundable)
//   asset_budget               10 XEL     earmarked for the protocol's asset
//                                         creation cost; unused part refunded
//                                         to the creator (D13)
//   min_liquidity            500 XEL     founder's locked seed liquidity
//   trading_fee_bps             50 bps    on every buy and sell while bonding
//   graduated_fee_bps           25 bps    curve trades between graduation and
//                                         migration (<= trading fee, D8)
//   migration_fee_bps           50 bps    taken ONCE from reserves at
//                                         graduation (D9), on both paths
//   direct_listing_threshold 2000 XEL     liquidity that skips bonding (D7)
//   recovery_fee              250 XEL     to re-open validation after trust
//                                         loss on a GRADUATED project
//   team_unlock_delay    3153600 topos    ~6 months of bonding before a
//                                         never-graduated team may claim (D3)
//   vesting bounds  518400..6307200 topos creator-chosen linear vesting
//                                         (~1 month .. ~1 year, admin-bounded)
//   validation window      51840 topos  ~3 days at ~5s per topoheight
//   min_participants            20      minimum voters to validate a project
//   min_approval_ratio_bps    8000      80% support required
//   graduation_multiplier        4      graduate at 4x the deposited liquidity
//   recovery_min_participants   40      stricter recovery quorum
//   recovery_min_ratio_bps     9000     90% support to recover Trust
//
//   LaunchDEX (the pool era): swap fee 30 bps default, capped 10%, 100%
//   admin — set on the DEX contract, cross-checked nowhere here by design
//   (the two fee models are independent venues; the graduation discount is
//   the curve's 25 bps window + the DEX's default being below the bonding
//   50 bps).
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SECURITY MODEL (honest threat documentation)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   * The admin is a hot role: it sets every fee/parameter, pins the DEX
//     (before the first migration only, D19) and can pause NEW proposals
//     and NEW buys. It can NEVER move curve reserves, token inventory,
//     team escrow or refundable rejections — withdraw_fees is capped at
//     pending_fees and at the contract's uncommitted balance (D20). Sells,
//     votes, refunds, migration and finalization are NEVER pausable:
//     exits, community decisions and the migration itself cannot be
//     frozen.
//   * The migration is permissionless and its outcome fully determined:
//     migrate() can only send the project's OWN reserves and inventory to
//     the PINNED DEX contract (D19) — no destination, no amount, no
//     caller choice anywhere. A malicious migrator can only... execute
//     the migration the community is waiting for.
//   * Cross-contract surface (the ONLY calls this contract ever makes):
//     LaunchDEX.create_pool (chunk 6) from migrate, LaunchDEX.
//     set_pool_buys_paused (chunk 7) from sync_trust_to_dex and from
//     migrate's untrusted-at-migration path. Both are inbound-guarded on
//     the DEX side (pinned launchpad address) and outbound-guarded here
//     (frozen dex pin, is_contract_callable permission precheck). The
//     calling transaction must carry the contract-call permission — the
//     clear "txperm" refusal documents it for wallets.
//   * Fee parameters are CROSS-CHECKED pairs: graduated_fee_bps <=
//     trading_fee_bps (D8) and direct_listing_threshold >= min_liquidity
//     (D7). Both setters read the partner value; the fee helper re-clamps
//     defensively at every use.
//   * Asset creation is balance-verified: if Fixed-mode semantics ever
//     delivered less than the full supply to this contract, finalize
//     reverts ("assetbal") — no partial-asset project can ever open.
//   * Voting sybil-resistance is the network fee, nothing more (documented,
//     not hidden). min_participants and the 80% bar make cheap attack
//     campaigns expensive: 20+ voting transactions, each paying network fees.
//   * Params are range-checked on every setter (hard caps in constants);
//     a compromised admin can hurt the fee model, not the funds.
//   * No reentrancy surface: XELIS invokes are atomic; this contract's
//     outbound calls happen last in their entries (state first), and the
//     two callees never call back (LaunchDEX calls no contract at all).
//   * Front-running buys/sells is possible (no mempool privacy) — same as
//     every public DEX on XELIS today; quotes are view functions, use them.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// INVARIANTS
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   I1. ASSET LEDGER (v4): for every created asset, the launchpad's
//       balance of that asset == curve_supply + team_remaining at EVERY
//       block — where team_remaining = team_alloc - team_paid. Tokens
//       leave the contract ONLY through buy payouts, sell... no: sells
//       ADD to the contract (the deposit). Tokens leave through buy
//       payouts and team claims ONLY; they enter through asset creation
//       (the full supply) and sell deposits. Post-migration the identity
//       degenerates to balance == team_remaining (the pool owns the
//       rest). Auditable by anyone: get_asset_info / get_balance_for_asset.
//   I2. XEL SOLVENCY (D20, tightened): contract XEL balance >=
//       total_curve_xel + pending_fees + locked_refunds + total_budgets
//       + total_vote_pots, before and after every entry — where
//       total_curve_xel is the exact sum of live curve reserves (seeds
//       included, minus rejected projects' refunds-in-waiting, minus
//       taken fees, minus migrated reserves), total_budgets the sum of
//       earmarked asset budgets, and total_vote_pots the sum of every
//       voter's refundable D21 deposit. Every XEL path updates both sides
//       atomically. Checked in withdraw_fees (the only exit path for
//       fees).
//   I3. A project's reserves can only grow by buy nets and shrink by sell
//       grosses, the one-time migration fee, and the migration itself;
//       the founder's liquidity only leaves via claim_refund on a
//       Rejected project, exactly once (with the unused asset budget).
//   I4. Team tokens are paid to the creator EXACTLY once across all claim
//       paths: every claim adds unlocked - team_paid and team_paid only
//       ever increases, capped at team_alloc.
//   I5. Every vote is one storage key ("v:{id}:{round}:{addr}") holding
//       the voter's LOCKED DEPOSIT AMOUNT (D21; 0 = voted for free) —
//       is_some() IS the "has voted" marker, the amount is what
//       claim_vote_deposit refunds (a claim zeroes it, keeping the marker
//       — the vote stays counted, the deposit leaves exactly once). An
//       address votes at most once per round; rounds only increase.
//   I6. Status transitions are one-way per path (see LIFECYCLE); nobody,
//       including the admin, can jump states arbitrarily. The migrated
//       flag is one-way: once set, the curve is closed forever.
//   I7. All transfers are checked (no swallowed failures). Every panic
//       message is a fixed short literal (no user data in panics).
//   I8. Untrusted blocks buys ONLY (D4) — on the curve directly, on the
//       pool via sync (D17). Sells and refunds always work, everywhere.
//   I9. Volume identity: per project, vo == bv + sv at ALL times; protocol
//       wide, tvl == tbv + tsv. The stored market cap mc is refreshed by
//       update_market_cap after EVERY change of its inputs, so it always
//       equals the recomputed R * circulating / C; mh only ever grows,
//       and mg is written exactly once, at graduation.
//   I10. TOKEN SOLVENCY: the migration sends EXACTLY the curve's
//       inventory (C) — the team escrow (team_remaining) never leaves
//       except through claims (I1/I4). A migration can never strand the
//       team or short the pool.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// STORAGE MAP (string keys, flat KV — house style)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   Global   : adm pc sub abd mnl tfe gfe mgf dlt mnp mab vdt gmu tdy vmn vmx
//              rfe rmp rmr pfe fcl tvl tcx lrf pz xa tbv tsv ttc tbb mgc dxa
//              vdp vote deposit (D21)   tvp total vote pots (D21)
//              (see constants below)
//   Project  : p:{id}:cr creator        p:{id}:st status (u64)
//              p:{id}:nm name           p:{id}:sy symbol
//              p:{id}:ds description    p:{id}:ws website
//              p:{id}:lg logo           p:{id}:tw twitter   (D11)
//              p:{id}:tg telegram       p:{id}:dc discord   (D11)
//              p:{id}:ts total_supply   p:{id}:tb team_bps
//              p:{id}:lq liquidity deposited
//              p:{id}:rv curve reserves p:{id}:cs curve token supply
//              p:{id}:ct created topo   p:{id}:ve validation deadline
//              p:{id}:sp supports       p:{id}:rp reports
//              p:{id}:gr graduated      p:{id}:rc refund claimed
//              p:{id}:rd vote round     p:{id}:vo trade volume (total)
//              p:{id}:dl direct-listing p:{id}:bt bonding start topo
//              p:{id}:tp team paid      p:{id}:vs vesting start topo
//              p:{id}:vd vesting duration
//              p:{id}:vp vesting PLAN declared at propose (D10)
//              p:{id}:bv buy volume     p:{id}:sv sell volume (D12)
//              p:{id}:tc trade count    p:{id}:lt last trade topo
//              p:{id}:mc market cap (stored spot, D12)
//              p:{id}:mh market cap ATH p:{id}:mg market cap at graduation
//              p:{id}:ah asset hash (set at creation, D13)
//              p:{id}:ab asset budget earmark (D13)
//              p:{id}:mi migrated flag  p:{id}:ma migrated at topo (D15)
//              p:{id}:mx migrated XEL   p:{id}:mt migrated tokens (D15)
//              p:{id}:ds dex trust synced flag (D17)
//   Votes    : v:{id}:{round}:{addr} -> locked deposit amount (D21;
//              u64 — is_some() is the vote marker, 0 = voted free,
//              claimed deposits are zeroed but kept)
//   Registry : t:{symbol} -> project id (ticker reservation, D11)
//   Reverse  : a:{asset_hex} -> project id (asset -> pid bridge, D22 —
//              written once at asset creation)
//   Migrated : m:{index} -> project id (migration order, D22 — written
//              once at migrate; pair with get_migrated_count)
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// EVENTS (V6 contract events: id + array of string fields)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//    1 ProjectCreated      [id, name, symbol, liquidity]
//    2 ProjectSupported    [id, round, voter]
//    3 ProjectReported     [id, round, voter]
//    4 ValidationFinished  [id, "1"|"0"]
//    5 BondingOpened       [id]
//    6 TokensBought        [id, xel_in, tokens_out, fee]
//    7 TokensSold          [id, tokens_in, xel_out, fee]
//    8 ProjectGraduated    [id, reserves, team_allocation]
//    9 TrustLost           [id, reports, supports]
//   10 TrustRecovered      [id]
//   11 FeesCollected       [amount]
//   12 ParamSet            [param, value]
//   13 Paused              ["admin"]        14 Unpaused ["admin"]
//   15 AdminSet            [new_admin]
//   16 RefundClaimed       [id, amount]
//   17 RecoveryRequested   [id, round]
//   18 ProjectInfoUpdated  [id]
//   19 TeamVestingStarted  [id, duration]
//   20 TeamClaimed         [id]                       — NO amount (D18)
//   21 DirectListed        [id, liquidity]
//   22 MigrationFeeTaken   [id, fee]
//   23 AssetCreated        [id, asset_hex, fee_paid]  (D13)
//   24 MigratedToDex       [id, xel_sent, tokens_sent] (D15)
//   25 DexTrustSynced      [id, "1"|"0"]              (D17)
//   26 DexAddressSet       [dex_hex]                  (D19)
//   27 VoteDepositClaimed  [id, round, amount]        (D21)
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CHUNK TABLE (entry-point IDs, 0-based, declaration order — CI-checked)
//    0   constructor                   1   only_admin                    2   require_project
//    3   proj_key                      4   vote_key                      5   fee_take
//    6   buy_tokens_out                7   sell_xel_out                  8   team_alloc_of
//    9   checked_add                   10  current_fee_bps               11  team_remaining
//    12  team_unlocked                 13  trust_guard                   14  take_migration_fee
//    15  update_market_cap             16  record_trade                  17  graduate
//    18  create_project_asset          19  migrate_to_dex                20  propose
//    21  support                       22  report                        23  finalize_validation
//    24  buy                           25  sell                          26  claim_refund
//    27  claim_vote_deposit            28  request_revalidation          29  update_project_info
//    30  start_team_vesting            31  claim_team_allocation         32  migrate
//    33  sync_trust_to_dex             34  set_submission_fee            35  set_trading_fee
//    36  set_graduated_trading_fee     37  set_migration_fee             38  set_direct_listing_threshold
//    39  set_min_liquidity             40  set_min_participants          41  set_min_approval_ratio
//    42  set_validation_duration       43  set_graduation_multiplier     44  set_team_unlock_delay
//    45  set_vesting_bounds            46  set_recovery_fee              47  set_recovery_params
//    48  set_asset_budget              49  set_vote_deposit              50  set_dex_address
//    51  set_admin                     52  set_paused                    53  withdraw_fees
//    54  get_project                   55  get_project_info              56  get_project_status
//    57  get_project_tokenomics        58  get_project_trust             59  get_bonding_info
//    60  get_current_price             61  get_buy_quote                 62  get_sell_quote
//    63  get_market_cap                64  has_voted                     65  get_total_projects
//    66  get_projects_by_status        67  get_project_by_rank           68  get_latest_projects
//    69  get_trusted_projects          70  get_trusted_by_rank           71  get_team_allocation
//    72  get_protocol_stats            73  get_config                    74  get_vote_config
//    75  get_recovery_config           76  get_team_config               77  get_social_links
//    78  get_trading_stats             79  get_market_cap_history        80  get_proposal_data
//    81  get_volume_stats              82  get_asset_info                83  get_project_by_asset
//    84  get_migration_info            85  get_migrated_count            86  get_migrated_by_rank
//    87  get_status_label              88  get_version
//
//   Auto-verified by scripts/verify_chunk_ids.py on every push: the table
//   above MUST match the declaration order in this file. Renumbering any
//   function invalidates the table — regenerate it, never hand-edit around.
// ============================================================================

